{"name":"Icy Waterfall","hex":"#c0d2d0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"icy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to, resembling, or abounding in ice; cold; frosty.","Covered with ice, wholly or partially."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/icy"},{"term":"waterfall","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flow of water over the edge of a cliff.","A waterfall-like outpouring of liquid, smoke, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fall like a waterfall.","To drink (something) from a container by pouring it from a height so as not to touch one's lips to the rim."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waterfall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Waterfall","blocks":[{"text":"A waterfall is any point in a river or stream where water flows over a vertical drop or a series of steep drops. Waterfalls also occur where meltwater drops over the edge \nof a tabular iceberg or ice shelf. Waterfalls can be formed in several ways, but the most common method of formation is that a river courses over a top layer of resistant bedrock before falling onto softer rock, which erodes faster, leading to an increasingly high fall. Waterfalls have been studied for their impact on species living in and around them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Cascada_Dynjandi%2C_Vestfir%C3%B0ir%2C_Islandia%2C_2014-08-14%2C_DD_136-138_HDR.JPG/330px-Cascada_Dynjandi%2C_Vestfir%C3%B0ir%2C_Islandia%2C_2014-08-14%2C_DD_136-138_HDR.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waterfall","wikidata":"Q34038"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Ulaan_tsutgalan%2C_Mongolia.jpg/500px-Ulaan_tsutgalan%2C_Mongolia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Ulaan_tsutgalan%2C_Mongolia.jpg/1280px-Ulaan_tsutgal